  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "The final rules keep S1 strict on reporting and customer notice. S2 sets a 55 °C test and a 5% failure benchmark but allows continued sale with corrective action and regulator discretion, while giving per-model failure rates to customers but not the public. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and retrofit within six years; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months; S5 sets an 8/100k threshold for notification and corrective-action plans but leaves recall to regulator discretion."
 },
